      \label{def weak bound on Laplacian}
Given functions $f,g:W\rightarrow \mathbb{R}$, we denote
\begin{eqnarray*}
        \Delta f \overset{w}{\leq} g 
        &\dot\Leftrightarrow&
        \int_W f\Delta\varphi \leq \int_W g\varphi ,
        \quad \forall \varphi\in C_c^\infty (W,\mathbb{R}^+).
\end{eqnarray*} 
In particular, a constant $\beta\in\mathbb{R}$ is called a \emph{weak bound on the Laplacian of $f$} if $\Delta f \overset{w}{\leq}\beta$

\begin{eqnarray*}
        \Delta f \overset{w}{\leq} g 
        &\dot\Leftrightarrow&
        \int_W f\Delta\varphi \leq \int_W g\varphi ,
        \quad \forall \varphi\in C_c^\infty (W,\mathbb{R}^+).
\end{eqnarray*}

